{
  "id": "rue-hab",
  "name": "Rue's hab",
  "description": "Rue's hanger: a shipping container converted into a one-room hab, open along its front and slung from the Spine's deck girders on heavy chains between Pylon Forty and Forty-One, a long way above the street. Chipped dark-green corrugated steel walls, an open grating floor. A narrow steel bunk with a tangle of blankets and a sleeping bag, and on a hook above it her dead father's olive hauler's jacket with its reflective stripe. A space heater glowing orange by the bunk. A desk of plastic crates and a plank: her deck, two cheap monitors of green code, a clamp lamp, a kettle, cups of instant noodles. A round porthole looks out at the next concrete pylon and its lit windows. Her boots, a coil of cable and a toolbox by the steel door, and outside the door the cable stair zigzags down toward Oksana's. Above and around, the underside of the highway and the lit windows of other hung habs.",
